  "facts": [
    "The Silvertown Tunnel, a 1.4 km twin‑bore opened on 7 April 2025, was delivered under a design‑build‑finance‑maintain contract by Riverlinx, a consortium including Cintra, BAM, Macquarie Capital and SK E&C.",
    "Construction employed an 11.87 m diameter earth‑pressure‑balance TBM named Jill after Jill Viner, London’s first female bus driver, and the tunnel’s segments were precast in Ireland by Banagher Precast Concrete.",
    "On 25 April 2025, a Critical Mass ride staged a mass trespass of roughly 1,000 cyclists, temporarily halting traffic and prompting TfL to close the tunnel for over an hour despite the ride lasting only ten minutes."
